# hello-prochat — environment variables
#
# ── 1. Model provider ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Pick ONE stanza below based on the `model:` in crewhaus.yaml.

# --- Anthropic (default) ---
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...

# --- OpenAI ---
# Set crewhaus.yaml `agent.model:` to e.g. `gpt-4o-2024-11-20`
# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...

# --- Google Gemini ---
# Set crewhaus.yaml `agent.model:` to e.g. `gemini-2.0-flash`
# GOOGLE_API_KEY=...

# --- AWS Bedrock ---
# Set crewhaus.yaml `agent.model:` to e.g.
# `bedrock/anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-20250514-v1:0`
# AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=...
# AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=...
# AWS_REGION=us-east-1

# ── 2. Code interpreter (Python / JavaScript / Shell) ────────────────
# These tools do NOT run in-process — @crewhaus/sandbox runs each call
# as a throwaway container (`docker run --rm -i --network=none
# --read-only --tmpfs /tmp --security-opt no-new-privileges <image>`).
# So a container runtime must be RUNNING or every call errors.
#
#   docker (default when unset) | podman | noop (disables the tools)
#
# Pre-pull the three pinned images before a demo — the first uncached
# call blocks on a multi-hundred-MB pull:
#
#   crewhaus sandbox doctor --probe
#     ✓ javascript node:22-alpine
#     ✓ python     python:3.13-slim
#     ✓ shell      alpine:3.19
#
# The images are pinned by @crewhaus/tool-code-execution and cannot be
# overridden from the spec. Python is the standard library ONLY — no
# numpy / pandas / matplotlib / scipy / requests, and --network=none
# means nothing can be pip-installed at call time.
# CREWHAUS_SANDBOX=docker

# ── 3. Image generation (/imagine) ───────────────────────────────────
# ImageGenerate resolves to the OpenAI provider whether or not a key is
# present. With NO key it errors — there is no built-in placeholder:
#   "OPENAI_API_KEY is not set — required for provider=openai."
# Set the key for real DALL-E output …
# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...
# … or force the offline text stub instead:
# CREWHAUS_IMAGE_PROVIDER=mock

# ── 4. Web search (/browse, WebSearch) ───────────────────────────────
# WebSearch dispatches to Brave or Tavily and needs BOTH vars. Without
# them it returns "WebSearch unavailable: set CREWHAUS_SEARCH_PROVIDER
# (brave|tavily) and CREWHAUS_SEARCH_API_KEY in the environment."
# WebFetch and Fetch need no credentials.
# CREWHAUS_SEARCH_PROVIDER=brave
# CREWHAUS_SEARCH_API_KEY=...
